<title>EGYPT: Yield falls on Egyptian three-month T-bills.</title>
<headline>Yield falls on Egyptian three-month T-bills.</headline>
<dateline>CAIRO 1996-11-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>The average yield on Egyptian 91-day treasury bills fell to 10.178 percent from 10.190 percent at the previous auction on November 14.</p>
<p>The Central Bank of Egypt announced the following details (values in pounds, previous auction in brackets):</p>
<p>Maturity date: Feb 20, 1997 (Feb 13, 1997)</p>
<p>Average yield: 10.178 percent (10.190)</p>
<p>Value of bids accepted: 656.350 million (679.550 million)</p>
<p>Value of bids: 700.950 million (826.575 million)</p>
<p>Range accepted: 10.002-10.204 percent (10.099-10.217)</p>
<p>Range of bids: 10.002-10.301 percent (10.099-10.572)</p>
<p>Number of bids accepted: 101 (222)</p>
<p>Number of bids: 115 (251)</p>
<p>($1 = 3.40 Egyptian pounds)</p>
<p>-- Cairo reporting unit +20 2 578 3290/1</p>
</text>
